>bill@snoopy (Bill Poitras)writes:
 
 >IMHO the most important factor in game design is fun factor.  I don't
 >care who gets the highest score, I like the game to be fun. Variety is 
 >the spice of life.  Making the game with various "tricks" might give a 
 >gamer more various ways to win some fun aspect of the game.  

   Well said. I wish that as much effort was spent making NetHack fun as
   is spent removing exploitable bugs, loopholes and generally attempting to
   make the game more difficult. I consider polypiling to be one of the 
   most fun features of the game. NetHack tends to generate an enormous 
   amount of junk items. It's immensely satisfying to turn all those black
   caps and mummy wrappings into something useful. There are already natural
   limits to polypiling. The most obvious being that one needs a lot of items
   to polypile. If one simply must restrict polypiling the best approach in my 
   mind would be to disallow polypiling wands into wands of polymorph.


